    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d202">

                <pb facs="0375" n="289" sameAs="frus:frus1945Malta/pg289"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The President’s Chief of Staff</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Leahy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the President
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-05">5 December
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Admiral Leahy to the President:</p>
                <p> Stettinius suggests that the following be sent to Prime today: President to
                    Prime.</p>
                <p>I have received from U. J. messages dated second and third December<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d202-f1"/> regarding his talks with de Gaulle and am informed he
                    sent you identical messages.</p>
                <p>I would like to have your views before I reply to Stalin. Roosevelt.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d202-f2"/>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
